WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.880
Good morning, John.

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.620
It's very nearly Thanksgiving here in these United States of America.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.040
According to Green family tradition,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.820
it's now time for me to tell you what I'm thankful for,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.120
which is a wonderful brother who is a brilliant writer,

00:00:11.129 --> 00:00:13.800
an awesome bunch of people who watch me make a fool out of myself on YouTube,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.920
an amazing family

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.120
and a loving wife,

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.180
who will carry my dead weight through all of Super Mario Brothers Wii.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.940
Now that my obligation to my mother,

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.620
who I love and am thankful for,

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.320
has been fulfilled,

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.240
I wanted to provide a service for the Google searching population of the world.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.260
At google, I typed in " Why are [SPACE]"

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.860
and I'm going to answer the top most searched-for question

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.360
for every single letter

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.200
of our alphabet,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.840
right now, starting now.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.980
"Why are asians so smart?"

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.140
Well first, even positive stereotypes are stereotypes. So you should be ashamed of yourself.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.440
But actually the theory on this subject, I think, that generally

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.380
Asian-American culture values smartness.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.340
And I think that our values as individuals

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.260
and as members of broader cultures

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.960
have a huge effect on what sort of people we end up becoming.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.760
Now. "Why are barns red?"

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.360
When farmers were treating their wood hundreds of years ago,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.200
they were doing it with the materials that they had at hand,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.100
and one of the materials that they had a hand was rust

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.780
and rust is a fungicide

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.900
and put that in the paint and it would prevent the wood from rotting.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.860
It also turned the wood kind of a rusty red-brown color.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.100
"Why are... Cuban cigars illegal?"

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.480
Fifty years ago,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.380
the Communist Cuban government decided that they owned all of the land that Americans owned in Cuba

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.120
and so they just took it.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:22.620
America was all,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.680
"C'mon give it back."

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.240
And then Cuba was like,

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.460
and then America was like,

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:26.960
"Fine.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.800
Then we're never gonna buy anything from you, ever again."

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.100
"Why are Dina and Caroline fighting?"

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.140
You know, I have no idea who those people are

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.980
but I'm just gonna venture a guess that it's because

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.940
they're not imagining each other complexly.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.160
"Why are enzymes important?"

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.060
Because every living thing on our planet is basically just a series of chemical reactions

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.840
and those chemical reactions are facilitated by,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.480
that's right, you guessed it,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.260
enzymes.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.180
"Why are flamingos pink?"

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.220
Because the food that they eat is pink.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.240
"Why are grapes bad for dogs?"

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.320
No one knows why grapes are bad for dogs,

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.540
but it's important to note that they are.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.960
Do not give your dogs grapes

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.380
and if they eat a bunch of grapes,

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.260
take them to the vet.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.040
"Why are Jews liberal?"

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.120
Really?!

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.900
"Why are Kardashians famous?"

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.100
Here's the thing about fame,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.420
we decide who's famous.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.780
I've decided that they aren't

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.620
so the Kardashians aren't famous,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.200
Cardassians are famous

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.640
they're infamous, in fact.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.580
"Why are leaves green?"

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.300
Because they're packed full of chlorophyll.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.780
"Why are manhole covers round?"

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.620
Well, one.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.940
Because sewers are round.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.740
And two.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.380
So that the manhole covers can't fall into the sewer.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.260
And three.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.420
To give douchebags an annoying and meaningless question to ask in job interviews.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.780
"Why are noble gases unreactive?"

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.620
Because their electron orbitals are filled.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:37.400
Duh.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.200
"Why are oceans salty?"

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.020
Fresh water falls on land and then as it runs down rivers,

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.367
it picks up tiny amounts of salt

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.100
and then it gets to the oceans, where it evaporates up

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.240
and the salt stays behind.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.280
Fresh water comes up,

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.800
more salt gets washed into the ocean,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.040
over eons and eons,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.260
salt builds up in the ocean.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.140
"Why are plants green?"

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.320
Already did that.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.180
"Why are q-tips called q-tips?"

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.960
And the q stands for quality.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.380
"Why are republicans stupid?"

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.600
Oh, come on, people.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.960
"Why are significant figures important?"

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.060
Cause measurement is entirely useless

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.940
without knowledge of the precision at which you are measuring.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.500
"Why are they called carpetbaggers?"

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.440
That's weird.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.900
Bring back the science.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.500
"Why are unions bad?"

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.080
Who told you unions were bad?

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.620
"Why are veins blue?"

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.120
They aren't blue and neither is deoxygenated blood,

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.120
subcutaneous fat in our skin actually blocks red light from escaping,

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.540
so you only see the blue light that's coming off of the veins,

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.040
huh?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.760
Interesting!

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.420
"Why are we here?"

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.380
Oh, Lord.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.620
You're asking Google?!

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.620
"Why our yawns contagious?"

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.740
So no one has any idea actually.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.900
"Why are zombies so popular?"

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.000
Well dear googler, in my opinion,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.660
it's because the myth of the zombie

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.660
allows us to do metaphorical battle with things that we cannot battle in real life,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.420
such as

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.020
disease

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:49.960
and decay

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.100
and violence

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.880
and the inevitable evacuation of ourselves

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.120
from our bodies.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.680
John, I will see you on Monday-

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:58.640
Wednesday-

